###
## The worker FSM, compiled to a raw BEAM `gen_statem` module and driven from
## Elixir by its atom (`:"Cure.Main.WorkerFsm"`).
##
## This is the live half of the pool: the Elixir `CurePool.Pool` GenServer owns
## the slot bookkeeping and supervises workers; each worker's lifecycle is this
## machine. The graph is verified at *Cure* compile time (see
## `cure/lib/worker_fsm.cure` for the annotated version); here the payload uses
## the BEAM-native shapes the Elixir side actually sends.
##
##   Idle --Reserve(client)--> Reserved --Activate(key)--> Active
##   Active --Return--> Returning --Reclaim--> Idle
##   Active --Timeout--> Returning
###

use Std.Fsm

rec WorkerData
  client: Atom
  key: Atom

fsm WorkerFsm with WorkerData
  initial Idle

  Idle --Reserve(client: Atom)--> Reserved
    update WorkerData{data | client: client}
  Reserved --Activate(key: Atom)--> Active
    update WorkerData{data | key: key}
  Active --Return--> Returning
  Active --Timeout--> Returning
  Returning --Reclaim--> Idle
    update WorkerData{data | client: :none, key: :none}
